d smart contract protocol on Ethereum.\n\nWithin hours, GitHub suspended the accounts of the core developers, deleted their code repositories, and revoked access to years of open-source documentation. Simultaneously, centralized RPC node providers like Infura and Alchemy blocked user requests interacting with the protocol addresses.\n\nThis event sent shockwaves across the software development community. It exposed a critical vulnerability in modern open-source development: **The code itself may be decentralized, but the tools, repositories, and communications used to build it remain deeply centralized.**\n\nIf a handful of corporate infrastructure providers can delete code repositories, revoke developer identities, or silence discussions at the request of state actors, then the software stack of the modern web is built on sand.\n\nBuilding true censorship resistance requires more than just decentralized money or permissionless social feeds. It requires **decentralized, uncensorable developer tools**.\n\n⚡ Zap 2100 sats to unlock the full article on\nhttps://fanfares.io/naddr/naddr1qvzqqqr4gupzpsz2urcgqnyttj5dl6l6zcjpg2ltk4vzl8rh5kla75jg8xcv645yqyvhwumn8ghj7enpdenxzun9wvhxummnw3erztnrdaksqfp3xy6rye3jxanz6ce5x4nz6dpk8qmj6ct9x5mz6er9xqckzvpn8y6kyvt9szag8u","created_at":1790895618,"id":"00b90d064519dedc492cff89783413c0a5740b47cd96da53de11341c42d5be82","kind":30023,"pubkey":"c04ae0f0804c8b5ca8dfebfa1624142bebb5582f9c77a5bfdf524839b0cd5684","sig":"88a7109cfc98a355614e10f2e85945cc63d1375bc9370ce8204442ae23874a3036e2510e6254d1d93d9463e2ed926b8a521e6ced5c0254adce4aa2efac76f498","tags":[["d","1142f27f-c45f-4687-ae56-de01a0395b1e"],["encrypted","aes-256-gcm","","https://api.fanfares.live/request-key"],["price","2100","SATS"],["a","31990:d7d8109ee43657ce6056ada4653006bbb641f31e50e85243681c2724507811ec:Fanfares","wss://fanfares.nostr1.com"],["client","Fanfares","31990:d7d8109ee43657ce6056ada4653006bbb641f31e50e85243681c2724507811ec:Fanfares","wss://fanfares.nostr1.com"],["X","b